# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the nightly libFuzzer run of fuzz_render.
# The target loads its fonts once, in LLVMFuzzerInitialize, and frees them at
# exit. Fontconfig holds those fonts' patterns and character sets behind
# encoded offsets, which LeakSanitizer cannot follow, so libFuzzer's check
# between inputs reports them as lost. Fontconfig's own default
# configuration, which Pango loads once on a thread of its own, is held the
# same way. Only allocations made under those two one-time setups are
# suppressed; a pattern or font set leaked anywhere else is still reported.
# A template matches any frame whose function name contains it, so the first
# line covers rmr_linux_fonts_create and rmr_linux_fonts_create_directory,
# the function the target calls. The replay tests run without these
# suppressions.
leak:rmr_linux_fonts_create
leak:FcInitLoadConfigAndFonts
